🔍 Important Difference from Day 10

In Day 10, you checked whether a number was a palindrome.

You had to manually reverse the number using:

digit = num % 10
r_num = r_num * 10 + digit
num = num // 10

In Day 16, strings make this much easier:

r_wrd = wrd[::-1]

So:

Day 10 → Number → mathematical reversal
Day 16 → String → slicing reversal

This is a good example of how Python provides different tools for different data types.


